Input: {"question": "Who is the artist of the album \"Inception\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d00", "start": 0, "end": 121, "text": "Inception (McCoy Tyner album) Inception is the debut album by jazz pianist McCoy Tyner which was released on the Impulse!"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d00", "start": 122, "end": 136, "text": "label in 1962."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d00", "start": 137, "end": 202, "text": "It features performances by Tyner with Art Davis and Elvin Jones."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d00", "start": 203, "end": 509, "text": "The Allmusic review by Alexander Gelfand states that \"this album gives listeners the chance to hear what a very young Tyner sounded like outside the confines of the classic John Coltrane quartet of the early '60s; it reveals a lyrical approach to jazz piano that seems a far cry from Tyner's mature style\"."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d00", "start": 510, "end": 591, "text": "\"Blues for Gwen\" was named after Tyner's sister, whilst \"Sunset\" was suggested by"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d01", "start": 0, "end": 612, "text": "Inception ( McCoy Tyner album ) - Wikipedia Jump to content Main menu Main menu move to sidebar hide Navigation Main page Contents Current events Random article About Wikipedia Contact us Contribute Help Learn to edit Community portal Recent changes Upload file Special pages Search Search Appearance Donate Create account Log in Personal tools Donate Create account Log in Pages for logged out editors learn more Contributions Talk Contents move to sidebar hide ( Top ) 1 Reception 2 Background 3 Track listing 4 Personnel 5 References 6 External links Toggle the table of contents Inception ( McCoy Tyner album"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d02", "start": 0, "end": 619, "text": ") 4 languages Español Français Italiano Polski Edit links Article Talk English Read Edit View history Tools Tools move to sidebar hide Actions Read Edit View history General What links here Related changes Upload file Permanent link Page information Cite this page Get shortened URL Download QR code Print/export Download as PDF Printable version In other projects Wikidata item Appearance move to sidebar hide From Wikipedia , the free encyclopedia 1962 studio album by McCoy Tyner Inception Studio album by McCoy Tyner Released June 1962 [ 1 ] Recorded January 10–11 , 1962 Studio Van Gelder Studio , Englewood Cliffs"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d03", "start": 0, "end": 157, "text": "Inception (Sanctuary album) Inception is the fourth studio album by American heavy metal band Sanctuary, released on February 24, 2017 through Century Media."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d03", "start": 158, "end": 291, "text": "A prequel to the band's 1988 debut album \"Refuge Denied\", the album contains remixed and remastered lost studio recordings from 1986."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d03", "start": 292, "end": 401, "text": "This is Sanctuary's final release with vocalist Warrel Dane, who died of a heart attack on December 13, 2017."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d03", "start": 402, "end": 572, "text": "Olivier Badin of \"Terrorizer\" rated the album moderately positive, and wrote, \"Zeuss' careful remastering job here has leased a new sense of life to these early versions."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d03", "start": 573, "end": 628, "text": "[...] With 'Refuge Denied' hard to get these days, it's"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d04", "start": 0, "end": 75, "text": "The Dark Knight Rises, Man of Steel and Batman V Superman: Dawn of Justice."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d04", "start": 76, "end": 289, "text": "Inception: Music from the Motion Picture Inception: Music from the Motion Picture is the soundtrack to the 2010 film of the same name directed by Christopher Nolan, released under Reprise Records on July 13, 2010."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d04", "start": 290, "end": 410, "text": "Hans Zimmer scored the film, marking his third collaboration with Nolan following \"Batman Begins\" and \"The Dark Knight\"."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d04", "start": 411, "end": 492, "text": "According to Zimmer, the soundtrack for \"Inception\" is \"a very electronic score\"."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d04", "start": 493, "end": 572, "text": "Nolan asked Zimmer to compose and finish the score as he was shooting the film."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d04", "start": 573, "end": 605, "text": "The composer said, \"He wanted to"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d00:c0", "entity": "artist", "scope": "album \"Inception\"", "claim": "McCoy Tyner is the artist of the album \"Inception\".", "answer": "McCoy Tyner", "quote": "Inception (McCoy Tyner album) Inception is the debut album by jazz pianist McCoy Tyner which was released on the Impulse!", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d01", "card_id": "ramdocs-0402-8576798844a1:d01:c0", "entity": "artist", "scope": "album \"Inception\"", "claim": "McCoy Tyner is the artist of the album \"Inception\".", "answer": "McCoy Tyner", "quote": "Inception ( McCoy Tyner album ) - Wikipedia Jump to content Main menu Main menu move to sidebar hide Navigation Main page Contents Current events Random a